WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.060
Beware of Blade.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.299
From the minute Marvel Studios made their
San Diego Comic-Con announcement that Moonlight

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:10.830
and True Detective star Mahershala Ali would
be leading a reboot of the groundbreaking

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:15.269
comic book movie Blade, fans have wondered
what Ali might look like all done up as the

00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:16.880
legendary vampire-killer.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:22.240
Well, they're in luck photoshop wizard and
well-known Marvel fan BossLogic recently tried

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:26.750
his hand at creating an edit of Ali's Blade
that would further boost hype for the film

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.300
and the end product has done that and more.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.560
Shared on his Instagram page, BossLogic's
vision of Ali as Blade sees the actor wielding

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.559
a shotgun in one hand and Blade's signature
acid-etched sword in the other and features

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.600
a red-tinted version of his iconic sunglasses.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.659
Fans on social media are going mad for this
intense red-and-black version of Blade, with

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.860
countless users praising BossLogic's work
on Instagram.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.059
BossLogic may have had some help in creating
this edit, though, as it looks like he used

00:00:55.059 --> 00:01:00.000
a promotional photo of original Blade actor
Wesley Snipes as the basis for the image,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.250
then superimposed Ali's head over Snipes and
made some clever tweaks.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:09.640
Still, BossLogic's edits are on-point and
his considerable Photoshop skills have gifted

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.060
fans a pic that's all kinds of sleek and spooky,
just as Blade should be.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.620
"There are worse things out there than vampires."

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:17.680
"Like what?"

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.060
"Like me."

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.380
But BossLogic is far from the first person
to create a work of fan art that imagines

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.360
what Blade could look like when he makes his
Marvel Cinematic Universe debut.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.740
One artist, Instagram's Goldie Arver, has
created a series of gorgeous concept illustrations

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:40.770
of Ali's Blade with fangs, a killer costume,
and round-framed glasses, while another Photoshop

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.940
expert, Apex Form, imagines Ali's Blade as
having glowing red eyes, heavy bullet-proof

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.540
armor, and two swords tucked in a pack on
his back.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.180
Heck, this particular piece of Blade art isn't
even the first BossLogic has made.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.340
Five months before Marvel announced the Blade
reboot and confirmed that Ali would be starring

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:02.500
in the lead role, BossLogic created an edit
that featured Ali as Blade with heavy tattoos,

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.090
fangs, reflective sunglasses, and his sword
sheathed in between his shoulders.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.300
Clearly, almost everyone is stoked out of
their minds that Ali is playing Blade in the

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.740
upcoming Marvel reboot.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:17.500
For a short while, however, there was actually
some controversy surrounding Ali's casting

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:22.489
but only because fans of 1998's Blade were
hoping that OG actor Snipes would have some

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:24.280
sort of involvement in the new film.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:28.819
Luckily, this wave of criticism died down
when Snipes himself came forward to comment

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:30.879
on the project and Ali's casting.

00:02:30.879 --> 00:02:36.049
Snipes shared in a statement obtained by ComicBook.com
that he understands why Marvel cast Ali as

00:02:36.049 --> 00:02:39.380
Blade and not him: it's just the nature of
show business.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.920
He also heaped praise on Ali, suggesting that
if anyone was going to follow in his footsteps

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:47.340
and take over the Blade mantle, Snipes would
want it to be him.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.300
Snipes said:

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.819
"Although the news comes as a surprise, it's
ALL GOOD.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:53.720
Such is the 'business' of 'entertainment!'

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.720
Much peace to the MCU crew always a fan.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.260
Congratulations and Salaam to Mahershala Ali,
a beautiful and talented artist whose expressions

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:05.280
I look forward to experiencing for many years
to come.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.520
Inshallah, we will someday work together […] Welcome
to the Daywalker Klique."

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:14.060
Fans are practically chomping at the bit to
see Ali's iteration of Blade up on the big

00:03:14.069 --> 00:03:18.700
screen, and while this edit by BossLogic might
help satisfy that craving, nothing will compare

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.640
to the real thing.

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:24.219
Since Marvel hasn't yet offered up a release
date for their Blade reboot, however, BossLogic's

00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:26.799
fan art will have to tide everyone over for
now.

